      "content": "thanks. that's a good start. one thing though—the board is pretty split. some members feel like the \"global accessibility\" argument is kind of a weak excuse to keep things that were basically stolen. can you expand a bit on why people on that side say the \"universal museum\" idea is actually outdated or even problematic? i want to make sure i'm hitting the critiques of the universalist view accurately.",
